# SYNTHETIC fixture, and one no prober can emit. It exists to be REFUSED.
#
# Construction, mechanical: prober/state/task-4-e2e/run-1.nq (run
# 2026-08-27T09:00:00Z, which measures all three endpoints and has an empty
# dormancy section) with a four-quad dormancy group for
# data.kkg.kadaster.nl/query spliced in after the header's sw:emission
# terminator, and the section's sw:dormantCount raised from "0" to "1" so the
# terminator still counts the groups before it.
#
# The result is ONE run graph that says both things about one endpoint: the
# sweep declined to ask kadaster, and the sweep measured kadaster. Those are
# opposite claims, a run graph is meant to describe one sweep's outcome, and
# whichever half a reader believes it is being told something the other half
# denies. web/load_run.py refuses it in _parsed_graphs, before the store is
# touched at all, naming the endpoint and the graph.
#
# Why it cannot come from the prober: the cadence decides once per endpoint per
# sweep whether to ask, and an endpoint it declined is never handed to a
# prober task, so no chunk is ever written for it. The refusal is not
# defending against this emitter; it is defending against a hand-edited file
# and against a future emitter whose two decisions have drifted apart.
#
# The four spliced quads use sw:dormancyReason "automatic", the other of the
# two reasons, so the committed fixtures cover both spellings.
#
# 166 quads, one run graph. Never load this file expecting success.
